# What the SDIST carries beyond the package itself.
#
# ⭐ WITHOUT THIS FILE THE RELEASED SDIST SHIPS A BROKEN TEST SUITE. setuptools' default sdist
# contents include `tests/test*.py` but NOT `tests/conftest.py`, so the tarball attached to every
# GitHub Release contained the tests and not the fixtures they depend on: two tests failed
# outright, and — the part that actually matters — the autouse fixture that makes "no test in this
# suite reaches the network" TRUE was simply absent from the artifact.
#
# That also quietly weakened the contract in README.md that "tests travel with the module", for
# anyone consuming the sdist rather than the repository. Tests that travel without their
# conftest have not travelled.
include MANIFEST.in
include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include pyproject.toml
include .leakguard.json
recursive-include tests *.py

# ⭐ `.leakguard.json` IS INCLUDED because it is an ARGUMENT for the tests, not decoration. This
# repository's own config is the worked example the leak-guard suite reads, and an sdist whose
# suite cannot find it ships tests that skip the one property the extraction exists to prove.
# Same failure as the missing conftest, one release later.
#
# ⛔ `scripts/` NO LONGER EXISTS, and the reason it was excluded is worth keeping because it now
# binds somewhere else. The guard used to be vendored there and was kept out of the sdist because
# its docstring enumerated the fleet's other repositories by name, which would have put that
# inventory inside every tarball attached to every public Release. The guard is now
# `src/kw_common/leakguard.py` — INSIDE the wheel, published to everyone who installs the
# library — so exclusion is no longer available as the fix. The names were removed from the file
# instead, and `test_the_shipped_guard_names_no_private_repository` is what keeps them out.
